  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3208.01 Required Certificates and Signs",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3208.01 Required Certificates and Signs.\n\n(a) Upon appointment, the inspection station owner shall prominently display the following certificates and signs to the public at all times:\n\n(1) A certificate of appointment for each type of inspection approved for the specific location;\n\n(2) Trade name shall be displayed clearly and conspicuously in letters no less than 10 inches in height, unless prohibited by local zoning; and such business signage shall be clearly visible from a traveling vehicle on the adjacent public way, unless an obstruction exists which cannot be remedied;\n\n(3) An official inspection station sign as set forth in Saf-C 3208.02; and\n\n(4) The inspection fee sign as set forth in Saf-C 3208.03.\n\n(b) This section shall not apply to authorized fleet inspection stations.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
